  "findings": [
    "N01 IN PERCEPTION (computed, at scale): over 50 probe-order permutations x both engines, every pair of orders yields a distinct information profile (min pairwise L2 2.41e-02 on L); max pairwise L2 0.8139 (L) / 0.8275 (R); final-chi spread 0.2344 (L) / 0.1543 (R). Commuting control (8 identical stages) is order-invariant to 0.0e+00 -- the order-dependence is carried by the stage64 generators, not the pipeline.",
    "perception quality depends on probe order: LOO bit accuracy across 50 orders spans [0.5312, 0.8906] on L (identity 0.7812) and [0.5156, 0.9219] on R (identity 0.8438); the v0 schedule is not optimal, just canonical.",
    "pysindy dI/dstage: held-out one-step R2 0.7431 with 7 active terms (library: poly deg 2 in I and stage covariates kappa/is_Dz/f; control input used=True); increment-scrambled control R2 0.7554. HONEST NEGATIVE: NO stage-specific law -- the increment-scrambled control fits as well as the real trajectories, so the R2 is carried by cumulative-series autocorrelation (I_[k+1] ~ I_k + drift), not by the stage covariates; the per-stage information-gain dynamics is not captured by a low-order polynomial law in (I, kappa, is_Dz, f).",
    "gudhi topology of perception: distinct register states per slot follow the bit lightcone exactly ([2, 4, 8, 16] at slots 0-3, prediction 2/4/8/16); H0 cluster partition matches a word class perfectly (ARI 1.0) at slots [0]; final-slot best ARI 0.0435 vs train_consensus_adm; total H0 persistence grows 0.8503 -> 6.0671 (cloud spreads as evidence accumulates); per-dimension scramble control mean best-ARI 0.0015 vs real 0.1400.",
    "qutip referee: 5 sampled words (['0100', '0111', '1010', '1100', '1101']) re-run with qutip mesolve (independent GKSL integrator, atol 1e-13) match the expm-superoperator engine at every one of 16 slots; max deviation 1.744e-11 (< 1e-8). The stage channels are integrator-independent.",
    "z3 POVM proofs (exact rationals): slot-0 ledger claims 64/120 pairs distinguished, slot-15 claims 120/120; all 12 sampled claims proven -- z3 finds a witness threshold POVM (observable + rational t) for each pair (SAT), and the erasure flip (both states averaged) is UNSAT in every case: no threshold POVM separates erased pairs."
  ],
